{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"content_hash":"16907fe07c4bb266d28d66d5996b9f9dfe9a0d925dbb68ba0e09c89b36b5cb0d","digest":{"component_or_area":"test infrastructure / conftest fixture","key_entities":["_rebar_repo_template","tests/interfaces/conftest.py","rebar.list_tickets()","rebar.init_repo()","pytest.MonkeyPatch.context()","tests/interfaces/test_rebar_repo_isolation.py::test_template_stays_virgin",".rebar","REBAR_ROOT"],"problem_keywords":["fixture assertion","template virginity","test isolation","ticket seeding","fixture construction"],"propositions":["The _rebar_repo_template fixture asserts no .rebar directory exists but does not assert the template contains no tickets.","A fixture-level assertion at construction protects all consumer tests and narrowed runs, whereas a separate test assertion protects only when that test is selected.","The missing tickets assertion must execute inside the MonkeyPatch context block where REBAR_ROOT and cwd are pinned, not after the context exits.","The assertion must call rebar.list_tickets() == [] to verify ticket absence without duplicating knowledge of store layout."]},"digest_hash_version":1,"model":"bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-opus-4-8","schema":"ticket_digest_v1"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"TICKET_DIGEST","timestamp":1787750332715515001,"uuid":"73bae90e-c4b4-4d6e-854f-b6f6b78763e5"}